{
    "openapi": "3.1.0",
    "info": {
        "title": "Alima API",
        "version": "1.0.0",
        "description": "Read access to an agency's clients, posts and connected channels, plus outgoing webhooks so another system can be told the moment something happens.\n\n**Authentication.** Every request needs `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. Tokens are created in Settings → Agent access and are the same tokens the MCP server uses. A token belongs to exactly one organization and that organization is never taken from request input, so there is no parameter that widens what a token can see.\n\n**Pagination.** Lists are cursor-paginated: read `meta.next_cursor` and pass it back as `?cursor=`. A null cursor means that was the last page. There is deliberately no total count — a reporting client walking the list while people are still creating posts would get rows skipped and repeated by offset paging, and could not tell.\n\n**Rate limit.** 300 requests a minute per token.\n\n**Errors.** Always `{\"error\": {\"code\": \"...\", \"message\": \"...\"}}`, except validation failures, which use Laravel's `{\"message\": ..., \"errors\": {...}}`.\n\n**Writes stop at a draft.** You can create and edit drafts and schedule an already approved post. Nothing can be created already scheduled, and scheduling re-runs the full pre-publish checklist server-side, so an integration cannot route around the approval step.\n\n**Idempotency.** Send an `Idempotency-Key` header (a UUID per operation) on every write. If your request times out you cannot tell whether it worked — retry with the same key and you get the original response back, marked `Idempotency-Replayed: true`, instead of creating a second post. Keys are honoured for 24 hours. Reusing one key for a *different* request body is a `409`, because answering it with the old response would hide a bug in your client.\n\n**Scopes.** `read` for every GET, `write:drafts` to create or edit a draft and to manage webhooks, `write:schedule` to schedule a post — the one write that reaches real audiences."
    },
    "servers": [
        {
            "url": "/api/v1"
        }
    ],
    "security": [
        {
            "bearerAuth": []
        }
    ],
    "tags": [
        {
            "name": "Identity"
        },
        {
            "name": "Clients"
        },
        {
            "name": "Posts"
        },
        {
            "name": "Channels"
        },
        {
            "name": "Webhooks"
        }
    ],
    "paths": {
        "/me": {
            "get": {
                "operationId": "me",
                "tags": ["Identity"],
                "summary": "What this token is and what it may do",
                "description": "The first call to make. Confirms the credentials work and names the organization they belong to, so a 403 elsewhere is something you can diagnose yourself.",
                "responses": {
                    "200": {
                        "description": "The token's organization and granted scopes."
                    },
                    "401": {
                        "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthenticated"
                    }
                }
            }
        },
        "/clients": {
            "get": {
                "operationId": "listClients",
                "tags": ["Clients"],
                "summary": "The roster this token can see",
                "parameters": [
                    {
                        "$ref": "#/components/parameters/PerPage"
                    },
                    {
                        "$ref": "#/components/parameters/Cursor"
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "status",
                        "in": "query",
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "string"
                        },
                        "description": "Only clients with this status."
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "archived",
                        "in": "query",
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "boolean"
                        },
                        "description": "Archived clients instead of active ones. They are kept, not deleted."
                    }
                ],
                "responses": {
                    "200": {
                        "description": "A page of clients."
                    },
                    "401": {
                        "$ref": "#/components/responses/Unauthenticated"
                    },
                    "403": {
                        "$ref": "#/components/responses/InsufficientScope"
                    }
                }
            }
        },
        "/clients/{client}": {
            "get": {
                "operationId": "getClient",
                "tags": ["Clients"],
                "summary": "One client",
                "parameters": [
                    {
                        "$ref": "#/components/parameters/ClientId"
                    }
                ],
                "responses": {
                    "200": {
                        "description": "The client."
                    },
                    "403": {
                        "description": "The client belongs to another organization, or to a client this token's member is not assigned to."
                    },
                    "404": {
                        "description": "No such client."
                    }
                }
            }
        },
        "/posts": {
            "get": {
                "operationId": "listPosts",
                "tags": ["Posts"],
                "summary": "What is planned and what went out",
                "description": "Each post carries its channels inline, because \"where did this go and did it work\" is the question being asked and fetching targets separately would be N+1 over HTTP.\n\nFor an incremental sync, pass `updated_since` and keep the highest `updated_at` you saw.",
                "parameters": [
                    {
                        "$ref": "#/components/parameters/PerPage"
                    },
                    {
                        "$ref": "#/components/parameters/Cursor"
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "client_id",
                        "in": "query",
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "integer"
                        }
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "status",
                        "in": "query",
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "string"
                        },
                        "description": "Archived posts are excluded unless you ask for `status=archived` by name."
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "updated_since",
                        "in": "query",
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "format": "date-time"
                        },
                        "description": "ISO 8601. Remember to URL-encode the `+` in an offset."
                    }
                ],
                "responses": {
                    "200": {
                        "description": "A page of posts, each with its channels."
                    },
                    "422": {
                        "description": "A filter was malformed — the body names which one."
                    }
                }
            },
            "post": {
                "operationId": "createDraftPost",
                "tags": ["Posts"],
                "summary": "Create a draft post",
                "description": "Needs the `write:drafts` scope. Always creates a **draft** — there is no parameter that creates something already approved or scheduled.\n\n`campaign_id`, `asset_ids` and every `channels[].social_account_id` must belong to the same client, so a token cannot borrow another client's campaign or media.\n\nEach channel carries its own local date and time; they are never shared implicitly. Attach media in the order you want it to publish — `asset_ids` is the carousel order.\n\n**Stories with a link or stickers.** Instagram only lets a person add a link, mention, hashtag, location or poll sticker from its own app. Set a channel's `format` to `story` and send `story_extras`, and that channel is **posted by hand**: Alima does not publish it. When it is due, someone on the team (or the client, see `handoff_recipient`) is reminded, posts it from Instagram and confirms it. The response says so with `posted_by_hand: true`. Extras on a channel that is not an Instagram story are a `422` on another network, and on an Instagram channel with another format are stored but change nothing.",
                "parameters": [
                    {
                        "name": "Idempotency-Key",
                        "in": "header",
                        "required": false,
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "maxLength": 255
                        },
                        "description": "A unique value per operation, e.g. a UUID. Retry with the same key to get the original response instead of repeating the work."
                    }
                ],
                "requestBody": {
                    "required": true,
                    "content": {
                        "application/json": {
                            "schema": {
                                "type": "object",
                                "required": ["client_id"],
                                "properties": {
                                    "client_id": {
                                        "type": "integer"
                                    },
                                    "caption": {
                                        "type": "string",
                                        "nullable": true,
                                        "description": "The master caption. Per-channel overrides are edited in Graphy."
                                    },
                                    "hashtags": {
                                        "type": "array",
                                        "items": {
                                            "type": "string"
                                        },
                                        "description": "Without the leading #."
                                    },
                                    "campaign_id": {
                                        "type": "integer",
                                        "nullable": true
                                    },
                                    "asset_ids": {
                                        "type": "array",
                                        "items": {
                                            "type": "integer"
                                        },
                                        "description": "Media to attach, in publish order."
                                    },
                                    "channels": {
                                        "type": "array",
                                        "items": {
                                            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ChannelInput"
                                        }
                                    }
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    }
                },
                "responses": {
                    "201": {
                        "description": "The created draft, with its channels.",
                        "content": {
                            "application/json": {
                                "schema": {
                                    "type": "object",
                                    "properties": {
                                        "data": {
                                            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Post"
                                        }
                                    }
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    },
                    "404": {
                        "description": "No such client for this token."
                    },
                    "409": {
                        "description": "The Idempotency-Key was reused for a different request, or one is still in flight."
                    },
                    "422": {
                        "description": "Validation failed — the body names the field."
                    }
                }
            }
        },
        "/posts/{post}": {
            "get": {
                "operationId": "getPost",
                "tags": ["Posts"],
                "summary": "One post with its channels",
                "parameters": [
                    {
                        "$ref": "#/components/parameters/PostId"
                    }
                ],
                "responses": {
                    "200": {
                        "$ref": "#/components/responses/Post"
                    },
                    "403": {
                        "description": "Not this organization's post."
                    }
                }
            },
            "patch": {
                "operationId": "updateDraftPost",
                "tags": ["Posts"],
                "summary": "Edit a draft post",
                "description": "Needs the `write:drafts` scope. Only ideas and drafts are editable; anything further along answers `409`, because a scheduled or published post being rewritten by an integration is a surprise nobody asked for.\n\nOnly the fields you send are changed. Sending `asset_ids` replaces the whole attachment list, in the order given.\n\nSending `channels` replaces the whole channel list: a channel you leave out is removed. A channel you list keeps its `format`, `story_extras` and `handoff_recipient` unless you send them, but its date and time are set from what you send, so send those every time. `story_extras: null` removes a story's extras, and it goes back to publishing itself.",
                "parameters": [
                    {
                        "$ref": "#/components/parameters/PostId"
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Idempotency-Key",
                        "in": "header",
                        "required": false,
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "maxLength": 255
                        },
                        "description": "A unique value per operation, e.g. a UUID. Retry with the same key to get the original response instead of repeating the work."
                    }
                ],
                "requestBody": {
                    "required": true,
                    "content": {
                        "application/json": {
                            "schema": {
                                "type": "object",
                                "description": "At least one of these.",
                                "properties": {
                                    "caption": {
                                        "type": "string",
                                        "nullable": true
                                    },
                                    "hashtags": {
                                        "type": "array",
                                        "items": {
                                            "type": "string"
                                        }
                                    },
                                    "campaign_id": {
                                        "type": "integer",
                                        "nullable": true
                                    },
                                    "asset_ids": {
                                        "type": "array",
                                        "items": {
                                            "type": "integer"
                                        }
                                    },
                                    "channels": {
                                        "type": "array",
                                        "items": {
                                            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/ChannelInput"
                                        }
                                    }
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    }
                },
                "responses": {
                    "200": {
                        "$ref": "#/components/responses/Post"
                    },
                    "403": {
                        "description": "Not this organization's post."
                    },
                    "409": {
                        "description": "The post is past draft, so it is not editable here."
                    },
                    "422": {
                        "description": "Nothing to update, or a field was invalid."
                    }
                }
            }
        },
        "/social-accounts": {
            "get": {
                "operationId": "listSocialAccounts",
                "tags": ["Channels"],
                "summary": "Connected channels and whether they are working",
                "description": "`connection_status` is the field to watch: \"why did nothing publish yesterday\" is almost always an expired token. No credentials of any kind are returned.",
                "parameters": [
                    {
                        "$ref": "#/components/parameters/PerPage"
                    },
                    {
                        "$ref": "#/components/parameters/Cursor"
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "client_id",
                        "in": "query",
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "integer"
                        }
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "platform",
                        "in": "query",
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "string"
                        }
                    }
                ],
                "responses": {
                    "200": {
                        "description": "A page of connected channels."
                    }
                }
            }
        },
        "/webhooks": {
            "get": {
                "operationId": "listWebhooks",
                "tags": ["Webhooks"],
                "summary": "This organization's webhook subscriptions",
                "parameters": [
                    {
                        "$ref": "#/components/parameters/PerPage"
                    },
                    {
                        "$ref": "#/components/parameters/Cursor"
                    }
                ],
                "responses": {
                    "200": {
                        "description": "A page of endpoints. Secrets are never included."
                    }
                }
            },
            "post": {
                "operationId": "createWebhook",
                "tags": ["Webhooks"],
                "summary": "Subscribe to events",
                "description": "Needs the `write:drafts` scope.\n\nThe response includes the signing `secret` **once**. Store it: it is never shown again, and it is the only way to tell a real delivery from a forged one.\n\nVerify a delivery by computing `HMAC-SHA256` over `\"{X-Alima-Timestamp}.{raw request body}\"` with the secret, and comparing the hex digest to the `X-Alima-Signature` header (which is prefixed `sha256=`). Reject anything whose timestamp is not recent.",
                "requestBody": {
                    "required": true,
                    "content": {
                        "application/json": {
                            "schema": {
                                "type": "object",
                                "required": ["url", "events"],
                                "properties": {
                                    "url": {
                                        "type": "string",
                                        "format": "uri",
                                        "description": "Must be https."
                                    },
                                    "events": {
                                        "type": "array",
                                        "minItems": 1,
                                        "items": {
                                            "type": "string",
                                            "enum": [
                                                "post.approved",
                                                "post.changes_requested",
                                                "post.published",
                                                "post.failed",
                                                "story.ready_to_post",
                                                "order.paid"
                                            ]
                                        }
                                    },
                                    "description": {
                                        "type": "string"
                                    }
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    }
                },
                "responses": {
                    "201": {
                        "description": "Created. Contains the secret, once."
                    },
                    "403": {
                        "$ref": "#/components/responses/InsufficientScope"
                    },
                    "422": {
                        "description": "A plaintext URL or an unknown event name."
                    }
                }
            }
        },
        "/webhooks/{endpoint}": {
            "get": {
                "operationId": "getWebhook",
                "tags": ["Webhooks"],
                "summary": "One subscription",
                "parameters": [
                    {
                        "$ref": "#/components/parameters/EndpointId"
                    }
                ],
                "responses": {
                    "200": {
                        "description": "The endpoint. `active` is false, with a `disabled_reason`, once it has been switched off after repeated failures."
                    },
                    "404": {
                        "description": "No such endpoint for this organization."
                    }
                }
            },
            "delete": {
                "operationId": "deleteWebhook",
                "tags": ["Webhooks"],
                "summary": "Unsubscribe",
                "description": "Needs the `write:drafts` scope. Its delivery history goes with it.",
                "parameters": [
                    {
                        "$ref": "#/components/parameters/EndpointId"
                    }
                ],
                "responses": {
                    "204": {
                        "description": "Gone."
                    },
                    "403": {
                        "$ref": "#/components/responses/InsufficientScope"
                    },
                    "404": {
                        "description": "No such endpoint for this organization."
                    }
                }
            }
        },
        "/posts/{post}/schedule": {
            "post": {
                "operationId": "schedulePost",
                "tags": ["Posts"],
                "summary": "Schedule an approved post",
                "description": "Needs the `write:schedule` scope — its own scope because this is the only write that reaches real audiences, and it cannot be undone by another call.\n\nThe post must already be **approved**. The full pre-publish checklist is re-run here, not trusted from earlier: if it does not pass you get a `409` whose `outstanding` array names every item still to fix.\n\n**Scheduled does not always mean it publishes itself.** A channel with `posted_by_hand: true` is an Instagram story with a link or stickers, which Instagram only allows from its own app. Alima does not publish that channel: a person is reminded when it is due, posts it from Instagram and confirms it. When a post has one, `meta.notes` carries a plain sentence saying so. Show it to whoever asked for the post to be scheduled. `meta.notes` is an empty array when every channel publishes automatically.",
                "parameters": [
                    {
                        "$ref": "#/components/parameters/PostId"
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "Idempotency-Key",
                        "in": "header",
                        "required": false,
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "maxLength": 255
                        },
                        "description": "A unique value per operation, e.g. a UUID. Retry with the same key to get the original response instead of repeating the work."
                    }
                ],
                "responses": {
                    "200": {
                        "description": "Scheduled. The post with its channels, plus `scheduled_at`, the earliest channel’s instant.",
                        "content": {
                            "application/json": {
                                "schema": {
                                    "type": "object",
                                    "properties": {
                                        "data": {
                                            "allOf": [
                                                {
                                                    "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Post"
                                                },
                                                {
                                                    "type": "object",
                                                    "properties": {
                                                        "scheduled_at": {
                                                            "type": [
                                                                "string",
                                                                "null"
                                                            ],
                                                            "description": "The earliest channel’s instant, UTC."
                                                        }
                                                    }
                                                }
                                            ]
                                        },
                                        "meta": {
                                            "type": "object",
                                            "properties": {
                                                "notes": {
                                                    "type": "array",
                                                    "items": {
                                                        "type": "string"
                                                    },
                                                    "description": "Plain sentences to pass on to a person. Empty when every channel publishes automatically.",
                                                    "example": [
                                                        "1 channel is a story on Instagram with a link or stickers. Instagram only allows those from its own app, so Alima will not publish it: someone posts it by hand from the Instagram app at 10:00 on 2027-05-04 (Europe/London), and is reminded at that time. Every other channel publishes automatically."
                                                    ]
                                                }
                                            }
                                        }
                                    }
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    },
                    "403": {
                        "description": "This token’s member may not schedule this post."
                    },
                    "409": {
                        "description": "Not approved yet, or the checklist did not pass (see `outstanding`)."
                    }
                }
            }
        },
        "/webhooks/{endpoint}/deliveries": {
            "get": {
                "operationId": "listWebhookDeliveries",
                "tags": ["Webhooks"],
                "summary": "What we tried to send you, and how it went",
                "description": "The dead-letter list. Every attempt is kept with its payload, response status, error and attempt count, newest first — so “did it arrive, and if not why” has an answer you can read without asking us.\n\nEach row carries the `payload` exactly as sent, which means you can reprocess a missed event straight from here without a replay at all.",
                "parameters": [
                    {
                        "$ref": "#/components/parameters/EndpointId"
                    },
                    {
                        "$ref": "#/components/parameters/PerPage"
                    },
                    {
                        "$ref": "#/components/parameters/Cursor"
                    },
                    {
                        "name": "status",
                        "in": "query",
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "enum": ["pending", "delivered", "failed"]
                        }
                    }
                ],
                "responses": {
                    "200": {
                        "description": "A page of delivery attempts."
                    },
                    "404": {
                        "description": "No such endpoint for this token."
                    }
                }
            }
        },
        "/webhooks/{endpoint}/deliveries/{delivery}/replay": {
            "post": {
                "operationId": "replayWebhookDelivery",
                "tags": ["Webhooks"],
                "summary": "Send a failed delivery again",
                "description": "Needs the `write:drafts` scope. Queues the delivery again with its **original** payload, `occurred_at` included: you are being told about something that happened then, not now.\n\nOnly a finished delivery can be replayed — one still working through its own retries answers `409`. So does a replay into a switched-off endpoint, which would fail immediately; re-enable it first.",
                "parameters": [
                    {
                        "$ref": "#/components/parameters/EndpointId"
                    },
                    {
                        "$ref": "#/components/parameters/DeliveryId"
                    }
                ],
                "responses": {
                    "200": {
                        "description": "Queued. The row is pending again."
                    },
                    "404": {
                        "description": "No such endpoint or delivery for this token."
                    },
                    "409": {
                        "description": "Still pending, or the endpoint is switched off."
                    }
                }
            }
        },
        "/webhooks/{endpoint}/enable": {
            "post": {
                "operationId": "enableWebhookEndpoint",
                "tags": ["Webhooks"],
                "summary": "Switch a disabled endpoint back on",
                "description": "Needs the `write:drafts` scope. An endpoint is switched off automatically after repeated consecutive failures, so a dead URL does not keep a queue busy forever. Once the URL works again, call this and then replay what was missed — your existing signing secret still applies, so there is nothing to reconfigure.",
                "parameters": [
                    {
                        "$ref": "#/components/parameters/EndpointId"
                    }
                ],
                "responses": {
                    "200": {
                        "description": "Active again."
                    },
                    "404": {
                        "description": "No such endpoint for this token."
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    },
    "webhooks": {
        "story.ready_to_post": {
            "post": {
                "operationId": "onStoryReadyToPost",
                "tags": ["Webhooks"],
                "summary": "A story is due and somebody has been asked to post it by hand",
                "description": "Sent once, when the first reminder goes out for an Instagram story with a link or stickers. Use it to route the reminder into your own tools. `url` opens the story inside Alima and needs a signed-in member; the reminder's own no-sign-in link is never sent to a webhook. Signed like every other delivery.",
                "requestBody": {
                    "content": {
                        "application/json": {
                            "schema": {
                                "type": "object",
                                "properties": {
                                    "event": {
                                        "type": "string",
                                        "enum": ["story.ready_to_post"]
                                    },
                                    "occurred_at": {
                                        "type": "string",
                                        "format": "date-time"
                                    },
                                    "organization_id": {
                                        "type": "integer"
                                    },
                                    "data": {
                                        "type": "object",
                                        "properties": {
                                            "post_id": {
                                                "type": "integer"
                                            },
                                            "client_id": {
                                                "type": "integer"
                                            },
                                            "post_target_id": {
                                                "type": "integer",
                                                "description": "The channel that is due."
                                            },
                                            "platform": {
                                                "type": ["string", "null"],
                                                "example": "instagram"
                                            },
                                            "handle": {
                                                "type": ["string", "null"]
                                            },
                                            "due_at": {
                                                "type": "string",
                                                "format": "date-time"
                                            },
                                            "posted_by": {
                                                "type": "string",
                                                "enum": ["team", "client"],
                                                "description": "Who was asked to post it."
                                            },
                                            "url": {
                                                "type": "string",
                                                "format": "uri",
                                                "description": "Opens the story in Alima for a signed-in member."
                                            }
                                        }
                                    }
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    }
                },
                "responses": {
                    "200": {
                        "description": "Any 2xx tells us it arrived."
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    },
    "components": {
        "schemas": {
            "StoryExtras": {
                "type": "object",
                "description": "What a person adds to an Instagram story by hand. Every key is optional; leave a key out, or send it as null, for an extra the story does not have. A placement note alone does not make a story posted by hand.",
                "properties": {
                    "version": {
                        "type": "integer",
                        "enum": [1],
                        "description": "Returned on reads. Ignored on writes."
                    },
                    "link": {
                        "type": ["object", "null"],
                        "description": "A link sticker.",
                        "properties": {
                            "url": {
                                "type": "string",
                                "format": "uri",
                                "maxLength": 2048,
                                "description": "Must start with https://."
                            },
                            "text": {
                                "type": ["string", "null"],
                                "maxLength": 30,
                                "description": "The sticker's own text."
                            }
                        }
                    },
                    "mentions": {
                        "type": ["array", "null"],
                        "maxItems": 5,
                        "items": {
                            "type": "string",
                            "pattern": "^@?[A-Za-z0-9._]{1,30}$"
                        },
                        "description": "Instagram handles. Returned without the @."
                    },
                    "hashtag": {
                        "type": ["string", "null"],
                        "maxLength": 100,
                        "description": "One tag, one word. Returned without the #."
                    },
                    "location": {
                        "type": ["string", "null"],
                        "maxLength": 80,
                        "description": "Free text. The poster picks the real place in Instagram."
                    },
                    "poll": {
                        "type": ["object", "null"],
                        "properties": {
                            "question": {
                                "type": "string",
                                "maxLength": 80
                            },
                            "options": {
                                "type": "array",
                                "minItems": 2,
                                "maxItems": 4,
                                "items": {
                                    "type": "string",
                                    "maxLength": 25
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    },
                    "placement_note": {
                        "type": ["string", "null"],
                        "maxLength": 280,
                        "description": "Where the stickers go, for the person posting."
                    },
                    "if_missed": {
                        "type": ["string", "null"],
                        "enum": ["fail", "publish_plain", null],
                        "description": "What happens if nobody confirms it in time. `fail` (the default) marks the channel failed and tells the team. `publish_plain` publishes the story without its link and stickers instead."
                    }
                }
            },
            "ChannelInput": {
                "type": "object",
                "required": ["social_account_id"],
                "properties": {
                    "social_account_id": {
                        "type": "integer"
                    },
                    "scheduled_local_date": {
                        "type": ["string", "null"],
                        "format": "date"
                    },
                    "scheduled_local_time": {
                        "type": ["string", "null"],
                        "description": "HH:MM on that channel’s own clock."
                    },
                    "format": {
                        "type": ["string", "null"],
                        "maxLength": 32,
                        "description": "The format this channel publishes as, e.g. `story`. Null lets Alima pick from the media. Must be one the channel's network offers."
                    },
                    "story_extras": {
                        "oneOf": [
                            {
                                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/StoryExtras"
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "null"
                            }
                        ],
                        "description": "Instagram only. With `format: story`, any extra makes this channel posted by hand."
                    },
                    "handoff_recipient": {
                        "type": ["string", "null"],
                        "enum": ["team", "client", null],
                        "description": "Who posts a story by hand. Null uses the client's default."
                    }
                }
            },
            "Channel": {
                "type": "object",
                "properties": {
                    "social_account_id": {
                        "type": "integer"
                    },
                    "platform": {
                        "type": ["string", "null"]
                    },
                    "handle": {
                        "type": ["string", "null"]
                    },
                    "status": {
                        "type": "string"
                    },
                    "format": {
                        "type": ["string", "null"]
                    },
                    "scheduled_local_date": {
                        "type": ["string", "null"],
                        "format": "date"
                    },
                    "scheduled_local_time": {
                        "type": ["string", "null"]
                    },
                    "scheduled_at": {
                        "type": ["string", "null"],
                        "format": "date-time"
                    },
                    "published_at": {
                        "type": ["string", "null"],
                        "format": "date-time"
                    },
                    "url": {
                        "type": ["string", "null"],
                        "description": "The live post. Always null for a story posted by hand: Alima cannot see it."
                    },
                    "error": {
                        "type": ["string", "null"]
                    },
                    "story_extras": {
                        "oneOf": [
                            {
                                "$ref": "#/components/schemas/StoryExtras"
                            },
                            {
                                "type": "null"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    "handoff_recipient": {
                        "type": ["string", "null"],
                        "enum": ["team", "client", null],
                        "description": "The channel's own choice of poster. Null means the client's default."
                    },
                    "posted_by_hand": {
                        "type": "boolean",
                        "description": "True for an Instagram story with a link or stickers. Alima does not publish this channel: a person posts it from Instagram when it is due."
                    },
                    "handoff_state": {
                        "type": ["string", "null"],
                        "enum": [
                            "needs_hand_posting",
                            "ready_to_post",
                            "posted_by_hand",
                            null
                        ],
                        "description": "`needs_hand_posting`: it will be posted by hand at its time. `ready_to_post`: it is due and somebody has been asked to post it. `posted_by_hand`: a person confirmed it went out. Null for a channel that publishes itself."
                    }
                }
            },
            "Post": {
                "type": "object",
                "properties": {
                    "id": {
                        "type": "integer"
                    },
                    "client_id": {
                        "type": "integer"
                    },
                    "campaign_id": {
                        "type": ["integer", "null"]
                    },
                    "status": {
                        "type": "string"
                    },
                    "caption": {
                        "type": ["string", "null"]
                    },
                    "channels": {
                        "type": "array",
                        "items": {
                            "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Channel"
                        }
                    },
                    "created_at": {
                        "type": ["string", "null"],
                        "format": "date-time"
                    },
                    "updated_at": {
                        "type": ["string", "null"],
                        "format": "date-time"
                    }
                }
            }
        },
        "securitySchemes": {
            "bearerAuth": {
                "type": "http",
                "scheme": "bearer"
            }
        },
        "parameters": {
            "PerPage": {
                "name": "per_page",
                "in": "query",
                "schema": {
                    "type": "integer",
                    "minimum": 1,
                    "maximum": 200,
                    "default": 50
                }
            },
            "Cursor": {
                "name": "cursor",
                "in": "query",
                "schema": {
                    "type": "string"
                },
                "description": "From the previous page's `meta.next_cursor`."
            },
            "ClientId": {
                "name": "client",
                "in": "path",
                "required": true,
                "schema": {
                    "type": "integer"
                }
            },
            "EndpointId": {
                "name": "endpoint",
                "in": "path",
                "required": true,
                "schema": {
                    "type": "integer"
                }
            },
            "DeliveryId": {
                "name": "delivery",
                "in": "path",
                "required": true,
                "schema": {
                    "type": "integer"
                }
            },
            "PostId": {
                "name": "post",
                "in": "path",
                "required": true,
                "schema": {
                    "type": "integer"
                }
            }
        },
        "responses": {
            "Post": {
                "description": "The post, with its channels.",
                "content": {
                    "application/json": {
                        "schema": {
                            "type": "object",
                            "properties": {
                                "data": {
                                    "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Post"
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }
            },
            "Unauthenticated": {
                "description": "Missing, unknown or revoked token."
            },
            "InsufficientScope": {
                "description": "The token does not carry the scope this endpoint needs. The message names it."
            }
        }
    }
}
